WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:02.900
[ YouTube Learning ]

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:04.540
Now that you have created a class

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:05.740
on Google Classroom,

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:08.300
let’s see how we can use Google Meet

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:09.880
to conduct a Live class!

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:13.980
[ Don't Memorise intro music ]

00:00:14.260 --> 00:00:16.220
The best way to conduct a Live Class,

00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:18.940
for your students is by using Google Meet

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:21.740
for which you need to generate a link!

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:23.600
How do we do that?

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:26.860
You can simply generate the Meet link by clicking here!

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:29.900
There you go, you have your meet link now!

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:31.880
You can choose to make the link visible to

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:33.400
students immediately,

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:35.800
or even on the day of your live class.

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:38.420
But there’s something really important you need to know

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:42.100
about Google Meet when you generate the link like this.

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:43.140
As a teacher,

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:46.080
you have complete control over your live class.

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:48.680
The students can enter the Google Meet class

00:00:48.680 --> 00:00:50.940
only after you have joined the class

00:00:51.080 --> 00:00:53.200
and can see who all have joined.

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:56.300
You can add or remove any of your students.

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:58.300
You can choose to put them on mute

00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:00.300
if there’s disturbance.

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:04.500
And the class ends, only after you decide to end it.

00:01:04.840 --> 00:01:07.000
Isn’t that amazing?

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.400
But remember, that all this will be possible

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:12.440
only if you generate the meet link by clicking here.

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:15.340
If you generate the Meet link using the calendar

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:19.720
or the app directly, these features may or may not work.

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:23.000
And Google Meet is also a very safe platform to use,

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:25.540
as nobody can attend your live online class

00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:27.120
without your approval.

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:29.060
Moreover, Google Meet works  on

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:32.260
smartphones, laptops, and tablets as well.

00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:34.460
Now that you know this,

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:38.100
let’s find out what all you could do using Google Meet?

00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:41.660
This is how your Google Meet screen would look.

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:43.160
You can look at the list of your students

00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:44.280
by clicking here.

00:01:44.680 --> 00:01:46.500
And these two buttons can be used to

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:49.980
switch your camera and mic on or off.

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:53.540
One of the most important things you can do

00:01:53.540 --> 00:01:56.700
is teach using a presentation you have already created.

00:01:57.300 --> 00:02:00.060
You could do this by Sharing your Screen.

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:01.420
All you have to do is click on the

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:02.980
‘Present Now’ button,

00:02:02.980 --> 00:02:05.240
and share the tab in which your presentation is open.

00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:08.500
Imagine how amazing it would be for the students

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:10.520
to view your beautiful presentation

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:12.580
while they are listening to you.

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:15.540
It could easily help the students make notes,

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:17.800
and also visualise better.

00:02:17.960 --> 00:02:19.060
And guess what;

00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:21.100
your students could also share their screens

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:24.360
if they want to share their work with the entire class.

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:27.780
Let’s stop this presentation now.

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:31.220
Alternatively, it could be a talking face live session

00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:34.000
where the students can just see you on the screen.

00:02:34.580 --> 00:02:37.260
You also have the option to hear and see

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:39.320
all your students on your screen.

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:41.600
I know you’d really like that but you should

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:43.880
know that it would consume more bandwidth,

00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:46.160
and hence it’s better that your students

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:49.300
are all on mute and have their camera disabled.

00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:52.260
But do you know how your students could still feel

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:54.300
involved in your session?

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:56.520
Yes, the chat feature.

00:02:56.740 --> 00:02:59.220
They can always ask questions, and post their thoughts

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:01.540
using the Chat option they see here.

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:03.100
And as a teacher,

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:05.300
you can answer them whenever you feel like;

00:03:05.380 --> 00:03:08.180
either immediately, or at the end of your session

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:10.420
And there are two more amazing features

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:13.480
of Google Meet that would help us teachers.

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:16.900
Did you know that you could also record your session?

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:20.540
Yes, by clicking on the Record Meeting button here,

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:23.520
your entire session could be recorded and then

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:26.040
shared with the students that missed your session!

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:27.980
Isn’t that amazing?

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:31.380
And now for one more super interesting feature!

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:34.220
If you turn on the Captions button here,

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:36.760
Meet automatically types out what you say

00:03:36.760 --> 00:03:39.280
and shows it to your students.

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:41.000
This could not only help students

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:42.840
who missed out on what you said

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:45.700
but also help students with hearing impairments.

00:03:46.220 --> 00:03:48.620
I know you must be waiting to get started.

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:49.880
In the upcoming videos,

00:03:49.880 --> 00:03:53.160
I will talk about how you could share content and create

00:03:53.160 --> 00:03:56.080
assignments for your students in Google Classroom

00:03:56.120 --> 00:03:57.960
See you there!

00:03:57.960 --> 00:03:59.400
[ #TeachFromAnywhere ]

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:07.980
[ YouTube Learning ]

